#
# Take client TLS handshakes off the accept loop's critical path. While
# the bridge waits for a client it now accepts everything queued on the
# listening socket and drives all of their handshakes side by side,
# pairing the first to finish; peers that never speak are shed at the
# handshake deadline without delaying anyone else, and without costing
# a server reconnect. See patches/README.md for the measurements.
#
